<title>FRANCE: Marseille tops French regional airports for airfreight.</title>
<headline>Marseille tops French regional airports for airfreight.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top ten regional airports for flown airfreight in January-February 1997, with percentage change on the same period last year, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  Marseille	    7,072  up    0.8</p>
<p> 2  Basle-Mulhouse*    6,498  down  6.0</p>
<p> 3  Toulouse	     4,166  down  1.0</p>
<p> 4  Lyon-Satolas	 3,664  up    6.0</p>
<p> 5  Lille**		3,664  up    3.0</p>
<p> 6  Nice		   2,666  up    2.8</p>
<p> 7  Bordeaux	     1,312	  0.0</p>
<p> 8  Strasbourg	     940  down  2.3</p>
<p> 9  Montpellier	    840  up    7.1</p>
<p> 10 Rennes		   665  up   78.3</p>
<p>*includes traffic  handled in Swiss zone of airport.</p>
<p>**also includes trucked air freight</p>
<p>The figures do not include France's major gateways for airfreight, Paris.CDG and Paris/Orly. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
